[{"text": "The assembly will now hear an address by", "start": 0.64, "duration": 5.96}, {"text": "his Excellency Irakli Kobakhidze,", "start": 2.56, "duration": 6.04}, {"text": "Prime Minister of Georgia.", "start": 6.6, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "I request protocol to escort his", "start": 8.6, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "Excellency and invite him to address the", "start": 10.88, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "assembly.", "start": 13.64, "duration": 2.52}, {"text": ">> Mr. President,", "start": 26.72, "duration": 1.48}, {"text": ">> [clears throat]", "start": 28.165, "duration": 1.875}, {"text": ">> Mr. Secretary-General,", "start": 28.2, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "Excellencies, distinguished delegates,", "start": 30.04, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "dear friends of Georgia,", "start": 33.12, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "it's a privilege to stand before this", "start": 35.04, "duration": 2.96}, {"text": "assembly", "start": 36.88, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "on behalf of Georgia, a nation shaped", "start": 38.0, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "by centuries of history,", "start": 41.24, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "resilience, and engagement with a", "start": 43.04, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "changing world.", "start": 45.52, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "We meet at a time of considerable change", "start": 47.76, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "in the international environment.", "start": 49.84, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "Developments in different parts of the", "start": 52.24, "duration": 3.48}, {"text": "world are challenging existing", "start": 53.76, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "arrangements and raising questions about", "start": 55.72, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "the future of the international order.", "start": 58.08, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "In this context, maintaining peace and", "start": 61.28, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "strengthening international cooperation", "start": 63.64, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "remain key priorities.", "start": 65.92, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "In light of the growing number of global", "start": 68.4, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "challenges, coordinated responses to", "start": 70.08, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "common obstacles, conflict prevention,", "start": 72.48, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "and the achievement of the 2030 agenda", "start": 75.08, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "for sustainable development are possible", "start": 77.52, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "only through strengthened international", "start": 79.8, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "cooperation and the shared commitment to", "start": 81.36, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "collective action.", "start": 84.04, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Lasting peace cannot be imposed by", "start": 86.2, "duration": 3.64}, {"text": "force. It must be built through", "start": 88.12, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "communication and mutual respect.", "start": 89.84, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "Few countries understand the value of", "start": 93.36, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "peace, stability, and sovereignty as", "start": 95.24, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "deeply as Georgia does.", "start": 97.6, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "For centuries, we stood at the", "start": 99.96, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "crossroads of civilizations, open to", "start": 102.0, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "diverse cultures, peoples, and ideas,", "start": 104.72, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "while steadfastly preserving our own", "start": 107.64, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "distinct identity and character.", "start": 109.48, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "Georgia's statehood has been tested more", "start": 112.68, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "than once, but these challenges have", "start": 114.48, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "only strengthened our determination to", "start": 116.8, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "choose our own path.", "start": 118.92, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "The trials of history have also taught", "start": 121.48, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "us that sovereignty can never be taken", "start": 123.28, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "for granted, that stability must be", "start": 125.64, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "protected, and the strength of the", "start": 127.64, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "international order ultimately depends", "start": 130.039, "duration": 4.361}, {"text": "on the same principles being upheld for", "start": 132.08, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "every nation.", "start": 134.4, "duration": 3.48}, {"text": "Our commitment to these principles", "start": 136.32, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "carries particular meaning for Georgia.", "start": 137.88, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "20% of our country remains under the", "start": 140.8, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "occupation of the Russian Federation,", "start": 142.84, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "while hundreds of our citizens continue", "start": 145.4, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "to live in displacement, unable to", "start": 147.76, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "return to their homes.", "start": 150.12, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "While restoring trust is a major theme", "start": 152.76, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "of this year's session,", "start": 155.0, "duration": 3.959}, {"text": "I would like to address our Abkhaz and", "start": 156.88, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "Ossetian brothers and sisters.", "start": 158.959, "duration": 4.281}, {"text": "We have shared a homeland and a history", "start": 161.24, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "for centuries.", "start": 163.24, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "The divisions of today cannot erase that", "start": 164.68, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "history, nor should they determine the", "start": 166.76, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "future of our children.", "start": 168.72, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "We believe that the dividends of peace", "start": 171.2, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "and economic growth of Georgia should", "start": 173.16, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "know no artificial boundaries.", "start": 174.959, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "It must reach the people living in our", "start": 177.64, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "occupied historic regions as well, who", "start": 179.6, "duration": 4.359}, {"text": "remain and will always remain part of", "start": 181.76, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "our shared future.", "start": 183.959, "duration": 3.881}, {"text": "The challenges facing our country also", "start": 186.16, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "remind us that national stability and", "start": 187.84, "duration": 3.8}, {"text": "success cannot be separated from the", "start": 189.92, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "wider regional context.", "start": 191.64, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "We believe that the South Caucasus", "start": 194.16, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "should not be defined by the divisions", "start": 195.76, "duration": 3.24}, {"text": "of the past.", "start": 197.72, "duration": 3.32}, {"text": "We have consistently sought to act as an", "start": 199.0, "duration": 4.519}, {"text": "honest broker in regional initiatives,", "start": 201.04, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "fostering cooperation and contributing", "start": 203.519, "duration": 4.681}, {"text": "to peaceful solutions.", "start": 205.64, "duration": 4.52}, {"text": "Today, we see a genuine opportunity to", "start": 208.2, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "turn a new page and build a more", "start": 210.16, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "peaceful and interconnected region based", "start": 212.08, "duration": 5.96}, {"text": "on shared commitment to a better future.", "start": 214.76, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "This spirit of cooperation must also", "start": 218.04, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "translate into tangible economic", "start": 220.2, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "opportunities for the region.", "start": 221.8, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "As an integral part of the South", "start": 224.48, "duration": 3.2}, {"text": "Caucasus and the middle corridor,", "start": 225.84, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "Georgia is well positioned", "start": 227.68, "duration": 3.4}, {"text": "to strengthen connectivity between", "start": 229.68, "duration": 3.8}, {"text": "Central Asia and Europe.", "start": 231.08, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "Our strategic location and direct access", "start": 233.48, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "to the Black Sea facilitate trade and", "start": 235.52, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "investment, linking landlocked countries", "start": 237.32, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "in our wider region to global supply", "start": 240.12, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "chains.", "start": 242.56, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "Our network of free trade agreements", "start": 243.84, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "provides access to a market of", "start": 245.84, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "approximately 2.3 billion consumers.", "start": 247.28, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "To support and further advance", "start": 250.92, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "connectivity agenda, Georgia plans to", "start": 252.28, "duration": 6.04}, {"text": "invest USD 7 billion by 2032 in major", "start": 254.48, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "transport infrastructure, modernizing", "start": 258.32, "duration": 4.52}, {"text": "the railway, developing the Anaklia deep", "start": 260.88, "duration": 3.4}, {"text": "sea port,", "start": 262.84, "duration": 2.92}, {"text": "building a new international airport in", "start": 264.28, "duration": 3.96}, {"text": "Tbilisi, and expanding the highway", "start": 265.76, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "network. At the same time, we believe", "start": 268.24, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "that physical and digital connectivity", "start": 270.84, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "are two parts of the same strategic", "start": 272.64, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "agenda.", "start": 275.12, "duration": 2.84}, {"text": "Through a Black Sea submarine fiber", "start": 276.24, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "optic connection and next-generation", "start": 277.96, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "data infrastructure, Georgia aims to", "start": 280.16, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "strengthen secure, resilient, and", "start": 282.56, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "diversified digital links between Europe", "start": 284.32, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "and Asia.", "start": 287.0, "duration": 3.24}, {"text": "These ambitions are underpinned by", "start": 288.6, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "Georgia's strong economic performance.", "start": 290.24, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "Over the past 5 years, our economy has", "start": 292.919, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "grown by an average of 9.3% annually,", "start": 295.36, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "and this momentum has continued in 2026", "start": 298.84, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "with growth reaching 7.9%", "start": 301.84, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "in the first 7 months of the year.", "start": 304.56, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "As the International Monetary Fund", "start": 306.96, "duration": 3.04}, {"text": "projects, Georgia will deliver one of", "start": 308.32, "duration": 3.32}, {"text": "the fastest growth rates in the medium", "start": 310.0, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "term among regional and European", "start": 311.64, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "countries, averaging 5.4%.", "start": 313.52, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "As one of the fastest-growing economies", "start": 317.44, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "worldwide, we are actively building an", "start": 319.12, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "innovation-oriented business-friendly", "start": 321.32, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "environment that supports both local and", "start": 323.16, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "foreign", "start": 325.72, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "enterprises. Despite the global", "start": 326.76, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "uncertainty, Georgia's FDI to GDP ratio", "start": 328.72, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "is one of the highest among peer", "start": 331.72, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "countries and averaged over 6% of GDP in", "start": 333.48, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "2021-2025,", "start": 336.76, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "highlighting the confidence of investors", "start": 339.12, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "in the country's growth potential.", "start": 341.24, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "Georgia's FDI outlook is supported by a", "start": 343.56, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "pipeline of large, multi-year investment", "start": 345.56, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "projects across transport and logistics,", "start": 348.0, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "energy infrastructure, tourism, and real", "start": 350.72, "duration": 3.48}, {"text": "estate.", "start": 352.8, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "Yet, the true measure of success is how", "start": 354.2, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "it improves people's lives.", "start": 356.16, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "Strong economic performance must", "start": 358.92, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "translate into tangible social outcomes,", "start": 360.44, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "higher output per person, rising real", "start": 363.04, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "wages, declining poverty, better", "start": 365.4, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "employment opportunities, and greater", "start": 367.84, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "economic resilience.", "start": 370.08, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "We're already seeing these outcomes", "start": 372.28, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "reflected in measurable improvements,", "start": 374.24, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "including a triple decline in Georgia's", "start": 376.28, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "poverty rate, which dropped from 21.3%", "start": 378.24, "duration": 7.6}, {"text": "to 7.1% since 2020.", "start": 382.28, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "Yet, this achievement is only part of", "start": 385.84, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "the broader transformation we seek to", "start": 387.44, "duration": 4.52}, {"text": "achieve.", "start": 390.4, "duration": 3.64}, {"text": "Over the next 5 years, our focus will", "start": 391.96, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "therefore be on narrowing disparities", "start": 394.04, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "between urban and rural communities,", "start": 396.12, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "expanding opportunities across every", "start": 398.76, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "region, and ensuring that the benefits", "start": 400.6, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "of economic growth are shared widely,", "start": 402.84, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "and that no one is left behind.", "start": 405.0, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "These priorities are fully aligned with", "start": 408.04, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "Georgia's commitment to the Sustainable", "start": 409.72, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "Development Goals, and are reflected in", "start": 411.76, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "our new United Nations Sustainable", "start": 414.16, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Development Cooperation Framework for", "start": 416.08, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "2026-2030.", "start": 418.24, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Looking further ahead,", "start": 422.08, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "our ambition for the coming decade is to", "start": 423.96, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "transform Georgia from an upper", "start": 425.96, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "middle-income country into a high-income", "start": 428.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "economy, underpinned by greater economic", "start": 430.12, "duration": 4.52}, {"text": "diversification, a growing share of", "start": 432.72, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "knowledge-based activities, and", "start": 434.64, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "broad-based prosperity.", "start": 436.56, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "Excellencies, ladies and gentlemen,", "start": 439.28, "duration": 4.2}, {"text": "the progress we seek at home is", "start": 441.919, "duration": 3.321}, {"text": "inseparable from the cooperation we", "start": 443.48, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "build beyond our borders.", "start": 445.24, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "Georgia remains open to meaningful", "start": 447.6, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "engagement with every international", "start": 449.28, "duration": 4.2}, {"text": "partner prepared to engage with us on", "start": 451.04, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "the basis of mutual respect and", "start": 453.48, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "sovereign equality.", "start": 455.6, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "We believe that lasting partnerships are", "start": 457.6, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "built through dialogue and never through", "start": 459.44, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "pressure or coercion.", "start": 461.64, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "The principles of respect and", "start": 464.08, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "cooperation are also at the heart of", "start": 465.64, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "effective multilateralism.", "start": 467.84, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "At the time of growing global", "start": 470.32, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "uncertainty, the United Nations remains", "start": 471.72, "duration": 5.32}, {"text": "indispensable as a forum for dialogue", "start": 474.68, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "and collective action.", "start": 477.04, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "In this regard, the UN 80 initiative", "start": 479.04, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "provides a valuable opportunity to", "start": 481.8, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "strengthen the effectiveness and", "start": 483.68, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "capacity of the United Nations while", "start": 485.36, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "further enhancing its transparency and", "start": 487.72, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "accountability.", "start": 490.16, "duration": 2.72}, {"text": "Georgia stands ready to work", "start": 491.56, "duration": 2.72}, {"text": "constructively with international", "start": 492.88, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "partners and contribute actively to this", "start": 494.28, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "process. We firmly support reforms that", "start": 497.2, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "will strengthen the organization's", "start": 499.72, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "capacity to deliver better and become", "start": 501.24, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "more results-oriented.", "start": 503.8, "duration": 4.119}, {"text": "The choice we make today will shape the", "start": 506.24, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "world we leave to future generations.", "start": 507.919, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "Let's ensure that we leave them a world", "start": 511.08, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "that is more peaceful, secure, and", "start": 513.599, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "united than the one we know today. Thank", "start": 516.0, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "you very much.", "start": 519.36, "duration": 2.559}, {"text": ">> [applause]", "start": 523.35, "duration": 2.02}, {"text": ">> On behalf of the assembly, I wish to", "start": 525.92, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "thank the Prime Minister of Georgia.", "start": 528.12, "duration": 3.719}]